{
  "version": 1,
  "board": "arduino:avr:uno",
  "control_period_ms": 5,
  "planning_notes": [
    "Board is Arduino Uno; D0/D1 are reserved for Serial and are not used.",
    "Two HC-SR04 sensors are declared as fully coherent acquisitions: vehicle uses Trig=D8/Echo=D9 and pedestrian uses Trig=D10/Echo=D11, each with a matching distance + validity request sharing the same physical trigger/echo pins.",
    "Ultrasonic sample_period_ms is set to 60ms to satisfy >= ceil((timeout_us+12)/1000) and >=60ms; the SysML model determines actual warning thresholds and the simultaneous-approach logic.",
    "LED pins: D12 is red and D13 is green, both active-high; SysML controls blinking/constant-on behavior.",
    "TM1637 uses CLK=D4 and DIO=D5; SysML maps danger level to the supported numeric range.",
    "Serial output reports only the most recent dangerous-event duration when the SysML boolean trigger asserts; value unit is ms.",
    "D2 is added as a digital_output to ensure the physical board pin required by the prior authoritative hardware configuration is owned by a catalog request; no further behavior is specified in the original requirements."
  ],
